---
description: When working on forms in project
alwaysApply: true
---

Reference implementation: app/assessments/components/assessment.form.tsx

Hook
- import { useForm } from '@/lib/forms/use-form'
- Available field components: TextField, TextareaField, DateField, SelectField, ComboField,
  CheckField, SwitchField, RadioField, FileField.

Field validation
- Use onChange validators for required fields so errors show inline as the user types.
- Do NOT add form-level validators to duplicate what field-level validators already check.
- Use form-level validators ONLY for cross-field rules (e.g. field B required when field A is set).
- Use form.Subscribe and useStore from tanstack for reactivity, avoid useEffect, useRef and similar.

Submit pattern
- Do NOT bind handleSubmit to the <Form> component.
- Each action button is type="button" with an explicit onClick handler.
- Read form.state.values directly inside the handler — no useRef, no hidden fields.
- Wrap mutation call in submitWrapper for automatic toast handling.

<Form> component
- Use <Form> from @/components/form as a layout wrapper only (no onSubmit prop needed).
- Use <FormActions> for the button row at the bottom.

User/profile picker
- Use useProfilesQuery() from @/lib/query/use-profiles for the options list.
- access details like userId, smfRoles and similiar from useUserModuleAccessContext().

Confirm dialogs
- Use <ConfirmModal> from @/components/ui/confirm-modal — there is no AlertDialog component, when applicable.


DYNAMIC TEMPLATE-RESPONSE FORMS
================================

Use this pattern for any form whose fields come from a document template
(sections → questions with dynamic response_type). Do NOT hand-roll
`useState<Record<questionId, value>>` for these surfaces.

Reference implementations
- Unified documents: app/documents/[id]/use-document-actions.tsx
  + document-detail.tsx
- Maturity assessments: app/assessments/assessment-instance-detail.tsx

Shared pieces
- Hook: `useTemplateResponseForm` from `@/lib/forms/use-template-response-form`
- Default Zod schema: `buildTemplateQuestionSchema` from `@/lib/forms/template-response-schema`
- Seed helper: `responseValueForQuestion` from `@/app/assessments/query/types`
  (accepts any TemplateResponseSeedRow — works for assessments, target markets, etc.)
- Wire converter: `inputForResponse` (assessments/TM) or `papStepInputForResponse` (step docs)

How to wire a surface
1. Call the hook with sections, responses, seed, and toInput:
     const { QuestionField, getResponseInputs, validateForSubmit, isValid, form } =
       useTemplateResponseForm({
         sections,
         responses,
         seed: responseValueForQuestion,   // or papStepResponseValueForQuestion
         toInput: inputForResponse,        // or papStepInputForResponse
         // buildSchema?: optional override of the default Zod builder
       });
2. Render each question with the returned QuestionField (not QuestionResponseField
   directly). Pass surface-specific passthrough props (disabled, evidenceContext,
   linkedEvidence, evidenceValue, onEvidenceChange, …):
     <QuestionField question={question} disabled={!editable} … />
3. Save: call getResponseInputs() inside the mutation handler (no separate values state).
4. Submit: await validateForSubmit() first; if false, toast and return. Inline errors
   are already shown on each QuestionField via FieldError. Then mutate with
   getResponseInputs() (save+submit in one click when the RPC accepts responses).
5. Keep surface-only state caller-side: evidenceValues map, confidentiality,
   changeReason, ConfirmModal open, etc. Merge those into toInput / the mutation
   payload — do not put them on the shared form.

What the hook owns
- Per-question TanStack Form field under `responses.<questionId>`
- Seeding once on mount (background refetches do not clobber edits)
- Per-field Zod validators (onSubmit only) from buildTemplateQuestionSchema
- getResponseInputs(), isValid, validateForSubmit()

What the hook does NOT own
- ActionMenuItem construction, ConfirmModal, ownership/RBAC gates
- Inline evidence ID maps (non-evidence response types)
- Confidentiality / change-reason / resubmit flows
- Read-only rendering of already-answered templates (pass precomputed `values`
  into a sections component without QuestionField — see TargetMarketTemplateSections)

Validation notes
- Validators run on submit only (via validateForSubmit), not on change or blur only for dynamic templates.
- Validators run on onChange for static forms.
- yes_no seeds as '' until the user explicitly picks Yes or No (false is a real answer).
- Table required-cell rules reuse tableRequiredCellsMissing inside the schema.
- Save/draft must NOT require validateForSubmit — only Submit/sign-off gates.
- Server-side RPC validation remains the source of truth; the schema is a UX layer.
- Custom required semantics: inject buildSchema, do not fork the hook.

Tests
- New schemas and formatters ship with a co-located test (`foo.ts` → `foo.test.ts`).
- Assert Zod `safeParse` on `error.issues[].path`, not message strings.

Bare form.Field
- Template questions intentionally use bare `<form.Field>` (not form.AppField) because
  field names are dynamic UUIDs. Static forms should keep using form.AppField with
  the registered field components listed above.
